Input: {"question": "Which award did Jean Marc Dalpé receive?", "original_source_segments": {"D1S1": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 0, "end": 164, "text": "As the snowflakes gently fell onto the cobblestone streets of Quebec City, Jean Marc Dalpé, the renowned Canadian writer, wrapped his scarf tighter around his neck."}, "D1S2": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 165, "end": 296, "text": "He had just received an unexpected letter from the Danish Embassy, inviting him to a prestigious ceremony at the Château Frontenac."}, "D1S3": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 297, "end": 419, "text": "The letter was cryptic, but the words \"Knight of the Order of the Dannebrog\" danced in his mind like a tantalizing melody."}, "D1S4": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 420, "end": 551, "text": "Jean Marc's thoughts wandered back to his childhood, spent listening to his grandfather's tales of Viking sagas and Nordic legends."}, "D1S5": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 552, "end": 700, "text": "His grandfather, a French-Canadian with a passion for Scandinavian culture, had instilled in him a deep appreciation for the region's rich heritage."}, "D1S6": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 701, "end": 815, "text": "As a writer, Jean Marc had often drawn inspiration from these stories, weaving them into the fabric of his novels."}, "D1S7": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 816, "end": 931, "text": "The day of the ceremony arrived, and Jean Marc made his way to the grand hotel, his heart racing with anticipation."}, "D1S8": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 932, "end": 1042, "text": "As he entered the opulent ballroom, he was greeted by the Danish Ambassador, resplendent in his formal attire."}, "D1S9": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1043, "end": 1196, "text": "The room was filled with dignitaries, writers, and artists from around the world, all gathered to celebrate the recipients of the Order of the Dannebrog."}, "D1S10": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1197, "end": 1382, "text": "As Jean Marc took his place among the honorees, he noticed a peculiar symbol etched onto the wall behind the podium – a stylized image of a Viking ship, its sails billowing in the wind."}, "D1S11": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1383, "end": 1483, "text": "He felt an inexplicable connection to the emblem, as if it held a secret message meant only for him."}, "D1S12": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1484, "end": 1579, "text": "The ceremony unfolded with precision, each recipient being called forth to receive their award."}, "D1S13": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1580, "end": 1707, "text": "When Jean Marc's name was announced, he rose from his seat, his eyes locking onto the Ambassador's as he approached the podium."}, "D1S14": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1708, "end": 1850, "text": "With a gentle smile, the Ambassador presented him with a delicate, ornate box adorned with the same Viking ship symbol he had noticed earlier."}, "D1S15": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1851, "end": 2130, "text": "\"Jean Marc Dalpé, for your outstanding contributions to literature and your dedication to promoting cultural understanding between our nations, we confer upon you the title of Knight of the Order of the Dannebrog,\" the Ambassador declared, his voice echoing through the ballroom."}, "D1S16": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2131, "end": 2217, "text": "As Jean Marc accepted the award, he felt a sense of pride and gratitude wash over him."}, "D2S1": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 0, "end": 15, "text": "Jean Marc Dalpé"}, "D2S2": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 17, "end": 101, "text": "Jean Marc Dalpé is a Canadian writer, born on September 21, 1957, in Quebec, Canada."}, "D2S3": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 102, "end": 211, "text": "He is a prominent figure in Canadian literature, known for his contributions to the country's literary scene."}, "D2S4": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 212, "end": 233, "text": "Early Life and Career"}, "D2S5": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 235, "end": 309, "text": "Dalpé was born in Quebec, Canada, and grew up in a French-speaking family."}, "D2S6": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 310, "end": 406, "text": "He developed an interest in literature at a young age and went on to pursue a career in writing."}, "D2S7": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 407, "end": 541, "text": "Dalpé's early works were heavily influenced by his Quebecois heritage, and he quickly gained recognition for his unique writing style."}, "D2S8": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 542, "end": 564, "text": "Literary Contributions"}, "D2S9": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 566, "end": 693, "text": "Dalpé's literary contributions have been significant, with a focus on exploring the complexities of Quebec's cultural identity."}, "D2S10": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 694, "end": 820, "text": "His works often delve into themes of identity, language, and culture, providing a unique perspective on the Quebec experience."}, "D2S11": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 821, "end": 958, "text": "Dalpé's writing has been praised for its lyricism, depth, and nuance, earning him a reputation as one of Canada's most respected writers."}, "D2S12": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 959, "end": 981, "text": "Awards and Recognition"}, "D2S13": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 983, "end": 1165, "text": "One of Dalpé's most notable achievements is receiving the Governor General's Awards, a prestigious Canadian award that recognizes excellence in academic, artistic, and social fields."}, "D2S14": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1166, "end": 1358, "text": "The Governor General's Awards are considered among the most esteemed honors in Canada, and Dalpé's receipt of this award is a testament to his outstanding contributions to Canadian literature."}, "D2S15": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1359, "end": 1384, "text": "Governor General's Awards"}, "D2S16": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1386, "end": 1575, "text": "The Governor General's Awards are a set of annual awards presented by the Governor General of Canada, recognizing excellence in various fields, including literature, music, and visual arts."}, "D2S17": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1576, "end": 1675, "text": "The awards were established in 1936 and are considered among the most prestigious honors in Canada."}, "D2S18": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1676, "end": 1724, "text": "Dalpé's Receipt of the Governor General's Awards"}, "D2S19": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1726, "end": 1848, "text": "Jean Marc Dalpé received the Governor General's Award for French-language drama in 1994 for his play \"Le chien\" (The Dog)."}, "D2S20": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1849, "end": 1970, "text": "This award is a testament to Dalpé's exceptional writing skills and his significant contributions to Canadian literature."}, "D2S21": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1971, "end": 1982, "text": "References:"}, "D2S22": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1984, "end": 2004, "text": "* \"Jean Marc Dalpé\"."}, "D2S23": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 2005, "end": 2031, "text": "The Canadian Encyclopedia."}, "D2S24": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 2032, "end": 2053, "text": "Retrieved 2022-02-20."}, "D2S25": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 2054, "end": 2093, "text": "* \"Governor General's Literary Awards\"."}, "D2S26": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", 